log}_{9}⁡x-8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+11{e}^{x},$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481479 1072 #uuid "24f4145d-a04e-5fb8-8280-a3728a721ed4" 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481479 1074 "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{log}_{9}⁡x-8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+11{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}-\\frac{8}{x}+11{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{5}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}-\\frac{8}{x}+11{e}^{x})\\,|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡9}-\\frac{8}{1}+11{e}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}-8+11e\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481480 1068 #edb/ref 17592186481476 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481480 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481480 1071 "Given the function  $y=8{log}_{4}⁡x-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+11{e}^{x},$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481480 1072 #uuid "3cd2bdcf-6143-519a-ac11-bbd298abfe66" 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481480 1074 "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{log}_{4}⁡x-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+11{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{9}{x}+11{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{8}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{9}{x}+11{e}^{x})\\,|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{9}{1}+11{e}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-9+11e\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481481 1075 #edb/ref 17592186481486 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481481 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481481 1077 "field-1" 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481481 1078 #edb/ref 17592186481486 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481481 1079 #uuid "71a8e926-e788-53c1-a4f8-cd5345e7fd65" 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481482 1080 "\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}12}-7+7e" 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481482 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481482 1083 #uuid "7cde23ae-bead-5869-9906-e9c6214c46d6" 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481483 1068 #edb/ref 17592186481487 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481483 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481483 1071 "Given the function  $y=3{log}_{6}⁡x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+8{e}^{x},$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481483 1072 #uuid "7f163702-82c3-5ed2-8962-43ef81d57fe6" 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481483 1074 "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{log}_{6}⁡x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+8{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}-\\frac{5}{x}+8{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}-\\frac{5}{x}+8{e}^{x})\\,|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡6}-\\frac{5}{1}+8{e}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}-5+8e\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481484 1068 #edb/ref 17592186481477 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481484 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481484 1071 "Given the function  $y=2{log}_{12}⁡x-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+7{e}^{x},$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481484 1072 #uuid "a17970fe-3001-5d61-8d91-323cad97da24" 13194139535219 17592186045443 true] [17592186481484 1074 "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{log}_{12}⁡x-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+7{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡12}-\\frac{7}{x}+7{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{